## Contracts

`contracts/openapi.yaml` is the composed source of truth for HTTP clients.
Edit `contracts/base/openapi.yaml` or `contracts/modules/*.yaml`, then run
`make contracts`; it recomposes the contract and regenerates the web
TypeScript types in `apps/web/src/contracts/schema.d.ts`.
`make contracts-check` fails when either the composed file or the generated
client is stale. `contracts/events.json` defines the agent streaming events.

`make contract-test` creates a scratch PostgreSQL database, starts the API,
grants the seeded admin role and runs Schemathesis against the live contract.
It fails on 5xx responses; missing fixtures and constrained-schema rejections
are warnings.

