## Web UI seam

The web app's visual seam is `apps/web/src/ui/`. Pages and features import
components only from there; `pnpm seam-check` (part of `make web-check`) rejects
a deep playbook visual import. Replace a component in that directory to
customize the UI without touching feature data flow. The chat surface on `/`
is the reference AI-native form; direct feature routes remain available.
Playbook package pages (for example the auth screens) are replaced at the route
level or by the package, not by a generated page.

The chat surface has a browser E2E with a mocked API:

```sh
pnpm --filter @{{ project_slug }}/web exec playwright install chromium
pnpm --filter @{{ project_slug }}/web test:e2e
# or: make web-e2e
```

Set `PLAYWRIGHT_CHANNEL=chrome` to use an installed Google Chrome instead of
downloading Chromium. CI installs the bundled browser.

The opt-in real-API E2E signs in, sends a run, submits feedback and loads the
learning dashboard without mocks. Start the API first, then:

```sh
make web-e2e-real E2E_USERNAME=<admin> E2E_PASSWORD=<password>
```
