## Agent runtime

The API plane owns AgentCore. With no model configured, the coordinator uses
deterministic single-step routing and each sub-agent runs its direct business
method. Set `CLIVER_AGENT_LLM_MODEL` plus `CLIVER_AGENT_LLM_BASE_URL` or
`CLIVER_AGENT_LLM_PROVIDER` (and the key) to enable LLM planning and the
sub-agent tool loop. The planner returns an ordered multi-step plan (one agent
per step, `CLIVER_AGENT_PLAN_MAX_STEPS`, default 8); later steps receive the
earlier steps' results as handoff. Each step runs one agent with its own
toolkit; skills are scoped to `skills/shared/` plus `skills/<agent-name>/` and
an agent may name its own MCP servers. Runs are durable: every event lands in
`agent_run_events`
before it is observable, one worker executes each run (streams only replay and
tail), the SSE frames carry `id: <sequence>` so `Last-Event-ID` resumes after a
reconnect, and keepalive comments cover quiet periods. A worker that vanishes
is marked `orphaned` rather than retried. Skills live in
`services/api/skills/`; tool definitions live on each sub-agent in
`services/api/app/agents/subagents/`. The UI never calls a model provider
directly.

Tool calls are scoped by `CLIVER_AGENT_TOOL_PERMISSION_MODE`: `scoped`
(default) allows declared builtin tools plus the selected MCP servers;
`read_only` also denies ASK-category tools; `allow_all` is the project
opt-out. A sub-agent's `AgentToolkit.allowed_tools` can narrow its own list.

Long runs can enable context compaction with
`CLIVER_AGENT_COMPACTION_ENABLED=true` (threshold
`CLIVER_AGENT_COMPACTION_THRESHOLD_TOKENS`, default 60000; keep
`CLIVER_AGENT_COMPACTION_KEEP_TURNS`, default 2). It summarizes older turns
through a separate tool-free model call when the previous call's input usage
crosses the threshold; it is off by default and requires the API-plane model.

MCP is opt-in. Put deployment server configs in a gitignored `.cliver/mcp.json`
(or point `CLIVER_AGENT_MCP_CONFIG` at a file) using the `mcpServers` shape,
then set `CLIVER_AGENT_MCP_ENABLED=true`. `${VAR}` values expand from the
environment, so tokens stay out of the file. Each sub-agent's `mcp_servers`
list is an allow-list; a per-run selector narrows it by intent. Discovery or
connection failures log and leave the run without MCP tools.

An optional System One/Laya selector narrows large tool and skill catalogues
before they reach the main model. It is fail-open and only activates above the
configured catalogue thresholds:

```sh
# Local laya (first run downloads the checkpoint)
CLIVER_AGENT_SYSTEM_ONE_PROVIDER=local make system-one-smoke

# Remote Aliyun Bailian
CLIVER_AGENT_SYSTEM_ONE_PROVIDER=bailian \
CLIVER_AGENT_SYSTEM_ONE_WORKSPACE_ID=<workspace> \
CLIVER_AGENT_SYSTEM_ONE_API_KEY=<dashscope-key> \
make system-one-smoke
```

Set `CLIVER_AGENT_JUDGE_ENABLED=true` to add a semantic LLM judge to
golden-set approval. It requires the API-plane model and fails closed when the
model is missing. Reviewer-gated staged rollout is available at
`POST /api/v1/agent/agents/{agent}/config/rollout` with a 0–100 percentage;
the overlay applies to a stable user/session bucket. Auto-apply remains off.

`CLIVER_AGENT_SYSTEM_ONE_PROVIDER` also accepts `typesafe` or `http`; leave it
empty to disable selection. `make system-one-smoke` is a live check and needs
the `local-system-one` extra for laya.
